WEBVTT

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:04.020
Endro!

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.780
I think this is getting out of hand.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:14.160
It's a strange sensation to recall memories 
of things I haven't experienced yet.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:15.880
Well, we've only remembered them.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.590
It's not as if our strength itself has changed.

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:20.540
So, what do we do, Yusha?

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:21.210
Huh?

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.040
Well, of course, we chase after 
her to rescue Rona-chan.

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:28.580
We're fighting Mao-sensei, then?

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:30.570
Or rather, the Demon Lord...

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:31.900
I don't know.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.430
But we can't just stay here and do nothing.

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:38.620
But we don't even know where they went.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:41.410
Looks like it's my turn, then.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:42.430
Sensei!

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:45.320
I heard a bit of what you were talking about.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:46.940
You're being vague again.

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:52.770
This Chaser Cartado will 
lead you to Mao-sensei.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:54.570
I use it all the time.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:57.830
That's a Cartado that gets my 
heart racing for many reasons.

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:00.740
Show us the path,

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:01.770
Chaser!

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.890
Looks like it's already picked her up.

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:09.190
All right! Let's go get our Princess!

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:09.840
Huh?

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:12.090
Y-Yeah...

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:13.950
Yulia-san.

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:14.840
Yes?

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:19.440
In some cases, such as when you 
lose your way in a dungeon,

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:23.230
going back to where you started 
is one viable solution.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:25.840
Back to where I started...

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:30.230
Demon Lord Castle

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:34.120
At this point, I'll just scatter those 
Heroes as a Demon Lord would

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:38.620
and turn all of Naral Island into the 
spitting image of pandemonium!

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:40.360
Please stop!

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:43.720
Even if you got too caught up
 in the flow to turn back,

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:46.280
Yusha-sama and the others 
are still your students!

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:48.300
You've said too much! Hmph!

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:52.180
Even you must have had an inkling 
that this would happen.

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:52.990
What?

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:53.630
Huh?!

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:56.320
I mean, you know, you...

00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:00.150
They might be surprisingly close by.

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:04.270
This is but another fate 
laid forth by the world.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:08.270
You got close to me saying ominous 
things like that, didn't you?

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:12.660
Oh!

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:17.500
That... was just me quoting
 the suggestive phrase used by

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:21.970
the Dark Knight in chapter 6 of 
volume 82 of the <i>Tales of Heroes</i>.

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:25.040
What the heck?!

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:29.210
My grandpa told me it was a phase 
all young people go through!

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:31.930
Besides, Sensei, the fact 
that you usually hide

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:36.300
that huge body in such an endearing form 
means you have a bit of that as well, right?

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:38.780
This one's my real form!

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:42.050
It's just... that other form is 
more Demon-Lord-like, isn't it?

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:44.210
So you were trying to look impressive?

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:45.810
Shut up!

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:51.060
Well, our Demon Lord also secretly 
composed poems in her secret room.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.710
How do you know that?!

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:57.570
Well, there's not a single thing
 I don't know about you, Demon Lord.

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:01.950
Oh? That's quite the boast, for a lowly golem.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:05.990
Since I'm a golem capable of 
operating semi-permanently,

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:07.830
I also know several truths

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:12.080
about the Heroes and Demon Lords 
that the Demon Lords don't know.

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:13.270
What was that?

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:15.300
What did you just say?!

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.150
As a Hero enthusiast, I can't let that go!

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:19.840
I don't mind.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:22.200
Just look at how lax the current Hero is.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.480
I doubt it's anything relevant.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:25.360
Then...

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:31.100
I never thought we'd be coming here again.

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:33.730
<i>We're coming for you now.</i>

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:47.860
That was a tough battle.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:51.250
Negotiating fees with 
higher penguins isn't easy.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:53.210
We're finally here.

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:55.480
It's the real Demon Lord's castle.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:04:00.090
It took a bit of time, and we ended 
up paying excessive fees, though.

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:03.090
Now that we're here,
 there's only one thing to do!

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:11.400
Camping outside the Demon Lord's 
castle is kind of thrilling.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:14.340
There's an elegance to viewing the 
moon at the Demon Lord's Castle.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:15.990
You're too calm about this.

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:18.730
The real Demon Lord is
 right around the corner.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:25.620
Do you think we really have 
to fight the Demon Lord?

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:29.470
That's what Heroes do, right?

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:32.370
You're right, but...

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:36.800
I know saying this now won't help,

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:40.300
but why did I want to be 
the Hero in the first place?

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:58.520
Welcome to the Demon Lord's castle, 
members of the Hero's party.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:00.780
Meigo-chan?

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:04.160
You're still calling me by that name?

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:07.280
When I'm a loyal servant of the Demon Lord?

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:09.860
Meigo-chan, did your memories...

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:13.040
No, you're you, Meigo-chan!

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:16.920
So you're saying Mao-sama is Mao-sama,
 not the Demon Lord?

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:20.200
How fitting for a Hero.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:23.580
You truly are kind and naïve.

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:27.490
Which is all the more reason 
for me tell you all.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:31.850
Long, long ago on Naral Island...

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:36.300
a great destructive power suddenly appeared.

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:38.990
Frightened, the people 
called it the Demon Lord.

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:44.650
Eventually, one who was known
 as the Hero defeated that power

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:46.320
and restored peace to the island.

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:50.250
However, the Demon Lord revived once more,

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:52.710
and so, too, did another Hero appear.

00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:57.260
That has repeated 998 times,

00:05:57.260 --> 00:06:00.590
leading to the current generation 
of the 999th Demon Lord.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.660
You know...

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:05.470
This Demon Lord reviving so 
much is a serious problem.

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:07.720
That's their destiny.

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:08.840
Huh?

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:11.740
The Demon Lord's power is far too great.

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:16.820
Even if they are defeated,
 they'll always regain their power and revive.

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:22.300
That's why they've been destined 
to revive and be defeated

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:24.430
before they can regain their power.

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:25.470
Hold on.

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:29.890
You mean the generations of Demon Lords
 aren't reviving on their own?

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:33.870
I don't know who prepared 
this destiny for them.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:39.350
All I know is that the Heroes have 
spent a long time wearing down

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:43.130
the power of those Demon Lords 
forced to revive prematurely.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:46.260
The Heroes are a part of that destiny, too.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:51.280
That's why they've conveniently revived at the 
same time as the Demon Lord's resurrection.

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:55.850
And you are the last Hero.

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:56.860
Huh?!

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:58.520
What do you mean, the last?

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:05.210
After 998 generations, that power has 
been worn down, and all that remains...

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:08.280
Well, to explain it more simply...

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:12.980
Once you all win, the Demon Lord 
will be eliminated for good,

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:15.160
never to revive again.

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:16.040
What?

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:20.670
You mean Mao-chan... will disappear?

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:22.000
Yes, yes!

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:24.100
I'm the last one, anyway!

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:26.420
Since I've been reborn only to be defeated,

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:29.590
it's better if the Hero just destroys me quickly!

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:32.830
<i>The Heroes I long admired</i>

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:39.480
<i>were just slaves to a destiny of 
wearing down the Demon Lord's power.</i>

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:44.060
<i>But if Yusha-sama and the others 
don't follow that destiny...</i>

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:48.060
<i>If Sensei, the Demon Lord, isn't defeated,</i>

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:50.650
<i>the Demon Lord will regain her full power</i>

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:53.740
<i>and try to destroy Naral Island once more.</i>

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:54.740
Hmph!

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:56.760
Yusha-sama...

00:08:00.470 --> 00:08:03.460
Jeez, my head's spinning.

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:07.180
So if we defeat the final Demon Lord,
 Mao-chan-sensei disappears,

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:10.260
and if we don't defeat her,
Naral Island will be wiped out.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:11.850
That's checkmate, isn't it?

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:15.220
Why did you go out of 
your way to tell us this?

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:16.260
Once we know this—

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:19.210
Yes, you won't fight.

00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:20.520
Not given who you are.

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:22.770
I knew it! You intentionally...

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:27.740
Right now, you all would fail to 
measure up to the Demon Lord.

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:31.780
However, you are the Hero,
so the improbable can happen.

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:34.550
Now, what will you do,

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:39.160
kind and naïve Hero of this generation?

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:45.720
Well, the Demon Lord is awaiting your visit.

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:51.910
Wh-What do we do?

00:08:51.910 --> 00:08:56.830
Whether we fight Mao-sensei or not, 
it's a tough decision to make.

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:58.830
We really are in checkmate, aren't we?

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:00.410
What do you think, Yusha?

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:01.620
Yusha?

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:04.270
Hey! Yusha!

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:04.720
Yu-chan!

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:06.100
Get a grip!

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:12.480
There was so much on my mind, 
I got overwhelmed for a second...

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:15.380
I guess it exceeded the limits
 of your processing power.

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:17.490
So, any good ideas?

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:19.340
Not at all...

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:21.860
My head just keeps spinning.

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:25.000
I'm at a total loss on what to do.

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:27.540
We're all lost in life!

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:31.000
Stop saying things that sound significant
 but don't mean anything.

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:36.010
Chibi-chan...

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:38.950
But I really am lost.

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:41.450
What would a Hero do?

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:45.520
When you lose your way...

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:48.810
When you lose your way...

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:54.580
They're late! Those guys are late!

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:56.860
Why haven't they come yet?!

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:57.950
Demon Lord.

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:00.890
There was a letter in the 
mailbox from the Hero.

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:03.390
Wait! Why does this castle have a mailbox?!

00:10:04.510 --> 00:10:05.710
Let's see.

00:10:05.710 --> 00:10:06.940
"Dear Mao-chan..."

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:08.830
<i>Dear Mao-chan!</i>

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:10.780
<i>It seems we've lost our way,</i>

00:10:10.780 --> 00:10:12.920
<i>so we're going to try
 going back to the start!</i>

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:14.710
What?! That idiot!

00:10:14.910 --> 00:10:16.160
Impressive!

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:20.470
Her actions are as unpredictable 
as the 518th Hero's!

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:22.400
Is this any time to be impressed?!

00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:24.470
You're being held hostage, you know!

00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:25.940
I'm sure...

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:28.320
she believes in you, Sensei!

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:31.980
She has faith that you won't hurt me!

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:40.090
I didn't raise her to be an adventurer
 that runs away from the Demon Lord!

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:44.180
I'll just have to go face her myself!

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:46.620
Let's go, Princess, Meigo!

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:49.380
Okay, Sensei!

00:10:50.510 --> 00:10:52.130
What's the matter, Meigo?

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:55.860
Come on! Hurry up and come with us!

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:58.380
Understood.

00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:09.560
This is where we started!

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:12.800
Both before and after we 
were flung into the past,

00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:15.070
we met here and formed our party.

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:20.070
And it was just because we happened to be 
in the same class and sat next to each other.

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:23.200
It wasn't very fateful.

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:27.920
Still, last time we all managed to make 
it to our fight with the Demon Lord.

00:11:33.340 --> 00:11:36.540
Because we all met here...

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:44.220
Seira-chan, what made you 
want to become a Priest?

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:44.850
Huh?

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:50.270
Both my mother and my grandmother
 came fom a long line of Priests.

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:54.130
It's a bond that's tied our family
 together for a long time... I guess?

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:56.880
What about you, Fai?

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:59.110
Why did you decide to become a warrior?

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:03.450
To protect the forest and my 
forest friends from bad people!

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:07.080
And you, Mei-chan?
 Why did you want to become a Mage?

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:10.280
Or so I thought I'd ask,
 but I guess it's because you love Cartado?

00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:12.980
That's right! That's why, but...

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:18.710
What about you, Yusha-san? 
Why did you want to become the Hero?

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:22.850
Yeah, I had forgotten why until just now.

00:12:22.850 --> 00:12:25.350
But I remembered after coming here.

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:29.470
My reason... was that it's cool!

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:32.150
What? That's too simple.

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:34.270
But it's a perfect fit for Yu-chan!

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:36.730
You're right. I can't see any other reason.

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:42.110
Oh, but there was one other reason!

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:44.360
So this is where you were?!

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:47.900
Yusha-sama!

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:49.500
Princess!

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:50.820
You're safe?

00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:53.530
Yes! I'm glad to see you're safe, too!

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:55.500
You're the one saying that?

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:58.830
Good grief, you're such bad students,

00:12:58.830 --> 00:13:01.010
causing so much trouble for me!

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:02.950
Mao-chan!

00:13:06.190 --> 00:13:08.800
Now, it's time for an extra lesson!

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:13.440
I'll show you the power of the Demon Lord
 you've all been wanting to fight!

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:15.500
Wait! We—

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:21.630
I won't say it again.

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:23.530
Draw your weapons.

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:25.400
Mao-chan!

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:30.630
I... no, we don't want to fight you, Mao-chan!

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:33.610
You are naïve!

00:13:33.610 --> 00:13:36.540
Is that what a Hero says to the Demon Lord?

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:37.540
No!

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:40.050
You're you, Mao-chan!

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:41.760
Our teacher!

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:42.830
That's right!

00:13:42.830 --> 00:13:46.760
You still taught us a lot, 
even knowing we were the Hero's party!

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:50.760
I learned a lot from you about 
Cartado and how to use them!

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:52.620
You were kinda scary when you got mad,

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:56.050
but you rewarded us when we worked hard,
 and that made me happy!

00:13:57.650 --> 00:14:00.600
We had fun with you, Mao-chan!

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:03.400
Was that not true for you?

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:06.240
Foolishness!

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:07.840
That's all...

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:12.390
That was all...

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:23.420
That was all ridiculously fun for me, too!

00:14:25.620 --> 00:14:31.930
But if I stay here undefeated, 
this island will be destroyed!

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:36.120
All that'll be left for me is eternal isolation.

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:40.980
Lonely, cold, and without anything else...

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:44.820
I can't stand that anymore.

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:52.700
In which case, it might not be so bad to 
be defeated by students I raised myself.

00:14:53.420 --> 00:14:54.610
Mao-chan...

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:57.710
All right.

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:03.380
Yusha!

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:03.380
Yu-chan!

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:03.380
Yusha-san!

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:07.700
I always wanted to be a cool Hero.

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:11.210
A cool Hero who took down 
the bad Demon Lord...

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:13.330
Demon Lord!

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:16.600
That's right. That's how it should be.

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:25.090
Chibi-chan, dinner time!

00:15:26.520 --> 00:15:27.110
Here!

00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:33.700
Burp.

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:38.140
Good!

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:40.710
What do you mean, "good"?!

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:44.150
What are you thinking?! 
That was the Hero's sword!

00:15:44.350 --> 00:15:48.150
Right! Without that sword,
 you can't be recognized as the Hero!

00:15:48.470 --> 00:15:49.940
Listen, everyone!

00:15:49.940 --> 00:15:53.490
The other reason I wanted
 to become the Hero was that

00:15:53.490 --> 00:15:56.340
I wanted everyone to have fun and be happy!

00:15:56.340 --> 00:15:57.220
That's why!

00:15:57.540 --> 00:16:01.280
And naturally, that includes
Mao-chan's smile, too!

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:08.110
If it means making Mao-chan cry, 
then I don't need to be the Hero!

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:12.610
Yulia Chardiet, you...

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:18.490
It's hard to say this while you're 
looking so accomplished, but...

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:20.290
Without the Hero,

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:24.130
Mao-chan-sensei's going to recover the 
power of the original Demon Lord

00:16:24.130 --> 00:16:27.000
and fulfill her destiny to destroy the island.

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:28.310
Huh?

00:16:28.310 --> 00:16:31.460
No way, that won't happen.

00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:32.760
Right, Mao-chan?

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:37.670
Huh?

00:16:39.270 --> 00:16:41.060
What do we do?!

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:43.710
That's my line!

00:16:44.090 --> 00:16:46.020
No, I've been waiting for this.

00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:55.530
Burp.

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:57.280
Huh?!

00:16:57.440 --> 00:16:59.570
You can't eat Mao-chan!

00:16:59.570 --> 00:17:01.110
Come on! Spit her out!

00:17:01.110 --> 00:17:02.640
You'll upset your stomach!

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:04.060
Don't eat food raw!

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:05.790
I don't think that's the problem here!

00:17:10.430 --> 00:17:13.170
Mao-chan! Thank goodness!

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:18.340
Hey! What did that beast just do to me?!

00:17:18.340 --> 00:17:23.780
You! You! You!

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:22.180
Please calm down, Demon Lord.

00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:25.810
More importantly,
 how is your power as a Demon Lord?

00:17:26.180 --> 00:17:27.180
Huh?

00:17:27.180 --> 00:17:30.080
Of course, it's still inside me...

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:31.550
It's gone?!

00:17:31.970 --> 00:17:32.740
Huh?!

00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:36.990
On that day of the final battle between 
the Demon Lord and the Hero's party...

00:17:39.020 --> 00:17:43.810
I got caught up in the Hero's 
forbidden spell, as well.

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:00.010
And...

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:08.100
while I was drifting in the gaps 
between dimensions, this one saved me.

00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:11.050
No, it didn't save you, it...

00:18:11.050 --> 00:18:13.010
You did good, Chibi-chan!

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:18.580
Normally it's impossible for 
a golem to move on its own.

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:21.940
However, this one made it 
possible for me to do so.

00:18:21.940 --> 00:18:23.220
Wait, wait, wait.

00:18:23.220 --> 00:18:28.450
So you're saying that thing ate the 
concept of "golem" attached to you?

00:18:28.450 --> 00:18:29.340
Yes.

00:18:29.340 --> 00:18:35.150
So I thought this one might 
also have the ability to erase

00:18:35.150 --> 00:18:40.890
the destiny of the Hero and Demon Lord 
by eating those concepts, as well.

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:43.940
And it seems like you were right.

00:18:43.940 --> 00:18:48.620
This was all thanks to Yusha-sama 
casting aside her role as Hero.

00:18:48.620 --> 00:18:50.140
Thank you very much.

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:51.260
Don't mention it!

00:18:51.260 --> 00:18:55.030
If everyone can have fun and smile, 
I'm perfectly okay with it!

00:18:55.480 --> 00:19:01.200
So the reason you told us all those things 
was so you could save Mao-sensei, too.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:05.230
That just shows how much 
Meigo-sama treasures Mao-sama!

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:10.790
Even if I couldn't move on my own, 
I was always watching her.

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:13.290
Uh, more importantly...

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:19.120
Erasing a concept from someone
 is a feat on par with creator gods!

00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:23.300
Why are you all keeping such a 
mysterious beast around as a pet?

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:27.180
Chibi-chan's your pet, right, Seira-chan?

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:29.280
Huh? I thought it was Mei's.

00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:33.600
Huh? I could have sworn Fai-san 
brought it with her from the forest.

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:36.730
Huh? There's nothing like her in the forest.

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:40.110
Besides, she's closest to Yu-chan.

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:43.790
Hey... How long has Chibi-chan been with us?

00:19:43.790 --> 00:19:47.800
Actually, I don't think she was with 
us on our adventures last time.

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:50.080
She was just kind of there one day.

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:53.900
Whatever!

00:19:56.180 --> 00:20:00.110
Good grief. What am I going to do with you all?

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:06.240
It's morning!

00:20:07.940 --> 00:20:10.940
I'm suddenly feeling tired.

00:20:10.940 --> 00:20:13.640
We were pretty busy all night long.

00:20:13.640 --> 00:20:15.520
I want to go home and sleep.

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:19.180
Don't you all be late for 
your first-period class.

00:20:19.180 --> 00:20:20.490
Huh?!

00:20:20.770 --> 00:20:22.100
Mao-chan, that's mean!

00:20:22.100 --> 00:20:24.500
You're going to make us attend like this?!

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:25.520
That's mean!

00:20:25.520 --> 00:20:27.520
Ogre! Devil! Demon Lord!

00:20:27.520 --> 00:20:30.500
Unfortunately for you,
 I've cast off being a Demon Lord!

00:20:31.220 --> 00:20:35.250
Oh, also, you all...

00:20:35.840 --> 00:20:37.630
What is it, Mao-chan?

00:20:38.010 --> 00:20:42.290
Uh, well, um, you know...

00:20:42.290 --> 00:20:44.140
Thanks for your help!

00:20:48.770 --> 00:20:51.400
Don't mention it! We're friends!

00:20:56.160 --> 00:20:58.180
Well, I'm off!

00:20:58.180 --> 00:20:59.820
Yes, Mao-sama.

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:00.400
Yeah!

00:21:01.090 --> 00:21:02.650
Take care.

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:05.410
Watch the house while I'm gone!

00:21:08.420 --> 00:21:10.690
Come on. Let's get going.

00:21:10.690 --> 00:21:13.160
We'll set a bad example 
as teachers if we're late.

00:21:14.480 --> 00:21:15.670
Right!

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:23.080
Hey, I heard they cleared an 
advanced quest the other day.

00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:25.050
That's the Hero's party for you.

00:21:25.300 --> 00:21:27.680
I bet they could defeat 
the Demon Lord now, too.

00:21:28.460 --> 00:21:30.570
Everyone keeps saying those things,

00:21:30.570 --> 00:21:33.920
but there's no Demon Lord
 or Hero anymore.

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:36.220
What's your job, Yusha-san?

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:40.190
I'm jobless, and you know it.

00:21:40.640 --> 00:21:43.980
But you can't accept quests if you're jobless.

00:21:43.980 --> 00:21:46.570
I know.

00:21:47.600 --> 00:21:50.180
Good morning, everyone!

00:21:50.180 --> 00:21:53.200
I know it's early,
 but please take a look at this!

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:55.820
Princess, what's that book?

00:21:55.820 --> 00:21:56.740
Right!

00:21:56.740 --> 00:22:00.220
This is the new <i>Tale of a Hero</i> that I created!

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:02.780
Let me see.

00:22:04.040 --> 00:22:04.970
Huh?

00:22:05.220 --> 00:22:07.270
It's just the cover right now.

00:22:08.320 --> 00:22:09.930
I got focused on the binding,

00:22:09.930 --> 00:22:12.220
and then I was satisfied with that on its own.

00:22:12.220 --> 00:22:13.300
That happens.

00:22:13.300 --> 00:22:14.480
Yeah.

00:22:14.670 --> 00:22:18.560
There are times when I'm satisfied 
just obtaining the Cartado I wanted.

00:22:18.560 --> 00:22:20.500
But then suddenly I remember that

00:22:20.500 --> 00:22:23.150
Cartado aren't just collectibles,
and that you can

00:22:23.150 --> 00:22:27.700
reach the depths of Cartado only 
when they're used by their owner.

00:22:27.700 --> 00:22:31.040
Then I realize how wrong I was
 to hold off using Imperial Feast

00:22:30.410 --> 00:22:32.000
It's blank.

00:22:31.040 --> 00:22:33.000
when I was trying to keep it unused.

00:22:32.000 --> 00:22:34.250
I'm sorry, Yusha-sama.

00:22:34.640 --> 00:22:36.620
Thank you, Rona-chan!

00:22:36.910 --> 00:22:37.520
Huh?

00:22:39.220 --> 00:22:42.420
Come on, now. Take your seats.

00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:43.920
Mao-chan!

00:22:44.460 --> 00:22:45.420
What is it?

00:22:45.760 --> 00:22:50.430
Our future is still blank, so we can 
become anything we want, right?

00:22:52.020 --> 00:22:53.680
I suppose so.

00:22:53.950 --> 00:22:55.620
In that case...

00:22:56.930 --> 00:22:58.810
I'm going to be the Hero!

00:23:01.040 --> 00:23:04.190
That's our Yusha. I thought you'd say that.

00:23:04.430 --> 00:23:06.820
That's just the way Yu-chan should be!

00:23:07.180 --> 00:23:08.820
I'll pal with you!

00:23:09.140 --> 00:23:10.820
Like a pal, hah!

00:23:11.060 --> 00:23:13.200
Wonderful, Yusha-sama!

00:23:16.060 --> 00:23:17.360
Chibi-chan!

00:23:17.360 --> 00:23:18.940
When did you get here?

00:23:18.940 --> 00:23:20.520
She pops in out of nowhere.

00:23:20.030 --> 00:23:21.580
Good grief.

00:23:20.520 --> 00:23:22.520
She's more mysterious than wacky seaweed.

00:23:24.180 --> 00:23:27.210
This is what's wrong with you Heroes.

00:23:27.600 --> 00:23:30.970
Well, I hope you give it your best.

00:23:31.250 --> 00:23:32.100
Yeah!

00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:34.910
I will!

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:39.980
Roll 12
